  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Removed:\n- MapTimeTz no longer offers the Func<TEntity, TimeSpan?> overload. PostgreSQL\n  timetz carries a UTC offset that a bare TimeSpan cannot supply, so the\n  overload could never write a valid value and threw at copy time. Map timetz\n  from a DateTimeOffset instead. This is source-breaking only for code that\n  referenced the removed overload; no working runtime scenario is affected.\n\nChanged:\n- MapTimeStampTz from a DateTime now requires DateTimeKind.Utc. A Local or\n  Unspecified value fails the copy with an InvalidOperationException that names\n  the offending column and states the UTC requirement, instead of leaking an\n  unqualified Npgsql error from deep in the COPY. For offset-bearing values,\n  use the DateTimeOffset overload of MapTimeStampTz.\n- The library no longer captures the caller's SynchronizationContext: every\n  await uses ConfigureAwait(false). Callers that block on the returned task\n  under a context that serializes continuations (classic ASP.NET, desktop UI)\n  no longer risk a deadlock, and continuations no longer marshal back to a\n  UI or request context.",
